---
description: Integration ("X to Y") pages under docs/integrations: structure, single source of truth, checks
globs: docs/integrations/**, docs/shared/integrations/**, src/data/integrations/**, src/components/integrations/**, scripts/integrations/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- One page per (source, engine) pair in `src/data/integrations/pairs.ts`. Add the pair there first, then `node scripts/integrations/scaffold.mjs <source> <engine>`.
- Pages compose components (`import * as I from '@site/src/components/integrations'`). Only the front matter, the intro, the methods table, the mechanism section, gotchas, troubleshooting and the FAQ are written per page. Setup steps come from `docs/shared/integrations` through `<I.Partial id="..." />`; a new partial is registered in `docs/shared/integrations/registry.ts`.
- Facts about what an engine reads (catalogs, delete formats, versions) live in `src/data/integrations/engines.ts` with the vendor page and check date. Never restate them inline on a page.
- Catalogs are always listed in the order from `catalogs.ts`: AWS Glue, Polaris, Lakekeeper, then the vendor-native ones.
- Every page needs a real run: `integration.tested` in the front matter with the date, OLake Go version, engines and the tested catalogs, plus screenshots of the real result. No run, no page.
- Front matter `integration:` must match `pairs.ts`. A page stays `unlisted: true` until the pair is `live` and `node scripts/integrations/check.mjs` passes.
- Tabs: `groupId="catalog"` with `queryString="catalog"` for catalogs (use `<I.CatalogTabs>`), `groupId="engine"` for the cross-engine section, `groupId="interface"` for UI versus CLI. Never invent a new groupId.
- Partials in `docs/shared` have no front matter and no H1.
- Writing: no em dashes, no paragraph over three sentences, every acronym expanded on first use, numbers only with a source or from the run, and OLake Go's limits stated plainly.
- Renaming or removing a page needs a redirect in `docusaurus.config.js` in the same change.
